{{Quote|Hey, Wannek. About your eye goggles. So, what, do you have poor eyesight?''"<br />"''They are for the protection&hellip;and the style.|[[ZO-E3]] and [[Wannek]]|<ref name="Vader Immortal Episode 3">{{VaderImmortal|III}}</ref>}}
[[File:MazKanataGoggles-SWBC57.png|thumb|250px|[[Maz Kanata]] wearing goggles]]
'''Goggles''' were protective wear for the [[eye]]s, typically worn for both military and civilian application. Goggles were typically used by riders of [[podracer]]s,<ref name="TPM">{{Film|I}}</ref> as well as by [[species]], like the [[Skakoan]]s, who found themselves in [[Atmosphere|atmospherically]] sensitive conditions.<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars">''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''</ref>

[[Rey Skywalker|Rey]] wore goggles made from old [[stormtrooper]] [[Stormtrooper armor|eyepieces]].<ref>{{WebCite|url=http://www.ew.com/gallery/star-wars-force-awakens-costume-gallery/2418343_rey|text='Star Wars' Costume Designer Breaks Down 'The Force Awakens'|author=Smith, C. Molly|date=2015-12-22|work=Entertainment Weekly|archivedate=20160927212445}}</ref> [[Tech]], a [[clone commando]] of [[Clone Force 99]], wore [[Color|yellow-tinted]] [[Tech's goggles|goggles]].<ref name="The Bad Batch (episode)">{{TCW|The Bad Batch (episode)}}</ref>

